---
/**
 * HeroDemo (DEMO-02): the home page's scroll-driven pair of thirty-second
 * stories. All markup and copy below is server-rendered static HTML - a
 * crawler sees the whole thing with no script running, per CLAUDE.md Part II
 * section 1.1. The only script this component ships is ScrollDriver.tsx,
 * which supplies motion only: every sentence a visitor reads exists in this
 * file regardless of whether that script ever runs.
 *
 * Content and structure were originally ported from a standalone mockup
 * (dirE.html). Revised 2026-09-04 per product-owner review of that first
 * pass, four directives: (1) the hero title and both captions were rewritten
 * to carry the errand and its outcome rather than describe the scroll
 * mechanic; (2) story one moved from Hebrew/RTL to English, and its arc was
 * extended to start at the incoming chat message and end at the OS share
 * sheet - `navigator.share`, what Sign actually calls - before the signed
 * file lands back in the thread; (3) story two now demonstrates all four
 * redaction tools (blur, blackout, whiteout, delete) each with a real effect
 * and a small chip naming it, instead of one fake "blur" that was a pale
 * highlight behind sharp text; (4) the palette stays Sea Glass throughout.
 * Losing the Hebrew field costs this site its one place where multi-script
 * support showed without being explained - the product owner's call, made
 * knowingly, not undone here.
 *
 * Second product-owner correction, same day: the permission slip's printed
 * sentence used to carry blanks for the trip's destination and times - the
 * school's own fields, filled in before the slip goes out - which read as
 * AI slop to anyone who has actually filled one of these out. Checked
 * against real field trip permission slip templates (Formstack, Jotform,
 * Vertex42, WeAreTeachers, Ninja Forms - search results 2026-09-04, no
 * single source copied) rather than guessed a second time: they agree on a
 * printed section covering destination, date, time and the class/teacher
 * running the trip, and a parent-filled section covering the student's
 * name, the parent/guardian's name, an emergency contact number, and any
 * allergies or medical conditions, ahead of the consent checkboxes and
 * signature. So the trip sentence ("Room 12 is going to the Science
 * Museum...") is now fully static printed text - it never changes during
 * the story - and the four blanks the parent fills are their own details
 * instead. The allergies/medical field is the most persuasive one on the
 * page for this product: it is exactly the line a parent would not want to
 * type into a site they have never heard of. See ScrollDriver.tsx's TRACKS
 * comment for the renamed beats.
 *
 * Track one (sign) gets the longer scroll length and goes first: a field
 * trip permission slip arrives as a chat attachment, gets filled in, ticked,
 * signed, shared, and sent back in the same thread. Track two (blur) is
 * shorter and second: a utility bill arrives by email and four lines get
 * blurred, blacked out, whited out and deleted before the reply goes out.
 * Both stories are mobile phone mockups.
 *
 * Scroll mechanic (ported from dirE.html, itself DEMO-05's pattern): each
 * story is a `position: sticky` panel pinned inside a much taller track
 * (672svh / 460svh, never 100vh - see CLAUDE.md's sticky-viewport-unit
 * note). ScrollDriver.tsx reads scroll position, computes 0-1 progress
 * through each track from getBoundingClientRect() every frame (never
 * accumulated, so scrolling back up genuinely un-fills the form), slices
 * that into named beat windows, and writes each as a `--p-<beat>` custom
 * property on the track's sticky stage element. HeroDemo.module.css never
 * hardcodes a beat boundary; it only ever reads whatever value shows up in
 * each property. See ScrollDriver.tsx for the beat map and
 * HeroDemo.module.css's "Layer visibility/crossfade" comment for how the
 * same mechanism produces a complete, non-blank finished frame under
 * `prefers-reduced-motion` and with JavaScript disabled - both are real,
 * required states, not degraded ones (see this ticket's acceptance).
 *
 * Zero-JS investigation (the ticket asks this be checked, not assumed):
 * CSS scroll-driven animations (`animation-timeline: scroll()` / `view()`)
 * could in principle replace ScrollDriver.tsx's rAF scroll listener with no
 * script at all. Checked against real support data (caniuse, 2026-09-03):
 * both landed in Chrome/Edge 115 (2023) and, critically for this mobile-
 * first product, in Safari 26 / iOS 26 (September 2025) - global usage
 * support is 87.01%, with Firefox not supporting either until version 158.
 * That is a real option, not ruled out on support grounds alone. It was not
 * taken here for three reasons specific to this component rather than a
 * blanket "not supported enough": (1) every one of the beats this component
 * drives would need its own `@property` registration (custom properties do
 * not interpolate as numbers without one - they flip at the midpoint instead
 * of easing) plus its own `@keyframes` and a positionally-matched
 * `animation-range`, which is a lot of new, first-of-its-kind surface in a
 * codebase whose CSS budget and duplication guards (CLAUDE.md Part II
 * section 6) already ratchet tightly; (2) shipping it *alongside*
 * ScrollDriver.tsx as a dual implementation - CSS for the ~87%, JS as a
 * fallback for the rest - means encoding the same beat boundaries twice, in
 * two languages that cannot check each other, which is exactly the
 * "duplicated math becomes impossible, single owner only" principle this
 * codebase already applies to gesture geometry (Part II section 3.2), just
 * expressed in timing instead of position; (3) writing `--p-*` custom
 * properties from a passive, rAF-throttled scroll listener is not a novel
 * technique here, it is the established "dynamic geometry" layer of the
 * styling boundary (Part II section 3.1) doing exactly the job it already
 * does elsewhere. Revisit if Firefox ships support and a second component
 * wants the same mechanic, at which point the duplication argument weakens.
 */
import ScrollDriver from './ScrollDriver';
import styles from './HeroDemo.module.css';

const rootSelector = `.${styles.root}`;
---

<section class={styles.root} aria-label="How PDkef works, shown as two short stories">
  {
    /*
      client:idle, not client:visible. ScrollDriver renders nothing (it
      only ever attaches a scroll listener to elements this file already
      rendered), so Astro mounts its <astro-island> as `display: contents`
      with no children - which has no box, so an IntersectionObserver-based
      client:visible never sees it as intersecting and the island never
      hydrates at all (verified in a real browser: getBoundingClientRect()
      on the island reports (0,0,0,0) regardless of scroll position).
      client:idle hydrates once the main thread is free, independent of
      layout or visibility, which is what a renderless island needs.
    */
  }
  <ScrollDriver client:idle rootSelector={rootSelector} />

  <div class={styles.hero} data-herodemo-intro>
    <h2 class={`type-section ${styles['hero-title']}`}>
      The form arrives in your chat. Finish it there and send it back.
    </h2>
    <p class={styles['privacy-line']}>Your document stays on your phone.</p>
    <div class={styles['scroll-cue']} aria-hidden="true">
      <svg class={styles['scroll-cue-icon']} viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" focusable="false">
        <path
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"
        />
      </svg>
      <span>scroll</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class={styles.track} data-hero-track="sign">
    <p class="sr-only">
      A field trip permission slip arrives as a file in a chat message. Tapping it opens the form
      right there in the chat. The form's printed heading, its sentence naming the trip's destination,
      date and times, and the checkbox labels are all there from the start, with blank spaces left for
      the student's name, the parent's name, an emergency contact number, and any allergies or medical
      notes. As the page scrolls, those four blanks fill in, both permission checkboxes get checked,
      and a signature draws itself on the line. A share sheet then slides up carrying the signed file,
      and back in the chat, the signed form goes out and reads as sent.
    </p>
    <div class={styles['stage-first']} data-hero-stage>
      {/* Inside the sticky stage, not above the track. As a sibling before
          it, the caption scrolled past in the first moments and the visitor
          then watched five screens of story with no idea what they were
          being told, and with no pause anywhere between the section title
          and the animation starting. Pinned here it holds for the whole
          story, which is both the pause and the context. It is absolutely
          positioned so it takes no part in the flex layout and the phone's
          height math is untouched; .stage-base reserves the room for it
          with --stage-caption-space. */}
      <h3 class={`type-card ${styles.caption}`}>Fill it in, sign it, and send it straight back.</h3>
      <div class={styles['progress-rail']} aria-hidden="true">
        <span class={`${styles['progress-seg']} ${styles['progress-seg-current']}`}></span>
        <span class={`${styles['progress-seg']} ${styles['progress-seg-pending']}`}></span>
      </div>
      <div class={styles['phone-first']} aria-hidden="true">
        <div class={styles.screen}>
          <div class={styles['status-bar']}>
            <span>9:41</span>
            <span class={styles['status-icons']}>
              <svg class={styles['icon-airplane']} viewBox="0 0 24 24" focusable="false">
                <path
                  fill="currentColor"
                  d="M21 16v-2l-8-5V3.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-3 0V9l-8 5v2l8-2.5V19l-2.5 2v1.5l3.5-1 3.5 1V21l-2.5-2v-5.5z"
                />
              </svg>
              <svg class={styles['icon-battery']} viewBox="0 0 24 12" focusable="false">
                <rect x="1" y="1" width="19" height="10" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" />
                <rect x="21" y="4" width="2" height="4" rx="1" fill="currentColor" />
                <rect x="3" y="3" width="14" height="6" rx="1" fill="currentColor" />
              </svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class={styles.layers}>
            <div class={`${styles.layer} ${styles['chat-layer']} ${styles['layer-final']}`}>
              <div class={styles['panel-head']}>Room 12 Families</div>
              <div class={styles.chat}>
                <div class={`${styles.bubble} ${styles['bubble-in']} ${styles['anim-msg']}`}>
                  <p class={styles['bubble-text']}>Hi all, the field trip permission slip is attached 🙏</p>
                </div>
                <div class={`${styles.bubble} ${styles['bubble-in']} ${styles['bubble-file']} ${styles['anim-msg']}`}>
                  <span class={styles['tap-ring']} aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <svg class={styles['pdf-icon']} viewBox="0 0 24 28" focusable="false">
                    <path class={styles['pdf-body']} d="M3 1h13l5 5v20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H3a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V2a1 1 0 0 1 1-1z" />
                    <path class={styles['pdf-fold']} d="M16 1v5h5" />
                    <rect class={styles['pdf-tag']} x="3" y="16" width="15" height="7" rx="1.5" />
                    <text class={styles['pdf-tag-text']} x="10.5" y="21.2" text-anchor="middle">PDF</text>
                  </svg>
                  <span class={styles['file-meta']}>
                    <span class={styles['file-name']}>field-trip-permission-slip.pdf</span>
                    <span class={styles['file-size']}>248 KB</span>
                  </span>
                </div>
                <div class={`${styles.bubble} ${styles['bubble-out']} ${styles['anim-send']}`}>
                  <svg class={styles['pdf-icon']} viewBox="0 0 24 28" focusable="false">
                    <path class={styles['pdf-body']} d="M3 1h13l5 5v20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H3a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V2a1 1 0 0 1 1-1z" />
                    <path class={styles['pdf-fold']} d="M16 1v5h5" />
                    <rect class={styles['pdf-tag']} x="3" y="16" width="15" height="7" rx="1.5" />
                    <text class={styles['pdf-tag-text']} x="10.5" y="21.2" text-anchor="middle">PDF</text>
                  </svg>
                  <span class={styles['file-meta']}>
                    <span class={styles['file-name']}>field-trip-permission-slip.pdf</span>
                    <span class={`${styles['file-status']} ${styles['anim-sent']}`}>Sent</span>
                  </span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class={`${styles.layer} ${styles['form-layer']}`}>
              <div class={styles['panel-head']}>field-trip-permission-slip.pdf</div>
              <div class={styles['tool-chips']} aria-hidden="true">
                <span class={`${styles['tool-chip']} ${styles['tool-chip-text']}`}>Text</span>
                <span class={`${styles['tool-chip']} ${styles['tool-chip-symbols']}`}>Symbols</span>
                <span class={`${styles['tool-chip']} ${styles['tool-chip-sign']}`}>Sign</span>
              </div>
              <div class={styles['doc-body']}>
                <div class={styles['doc-heading']}>Field Trip Permission Slip</div>
                <p class={styles['trip-sentence']}>
                  Room 12 is going to the Science Museum on Friday, May 14, from 8:00 AM to 3:30 PM.
                </p>
                <div class={styles['parent-fields']}>
                  <div class={styles['field-row']}>
                    <span class={styles['field-label']}>Student's Name</span>
                    <span class={styles['blank-name']}
                      ><span class={`${styles['blank-value']} ${styles['blank-value-name']}`}>Maya Chen</span></span
                    >
                  </div>
                  <div class={styles['field-row']}>
                    <span class={styles['field-label']}>Parent/Guardian</span>
                    <span class={styles['blank-guardian']}
                      ><span class={`${styles['blank-value']} ${styles['blank-value-guardian']}`}>Elena Chen</span
                      ></span
                    >
                  </div>
                  <div class={styles['field-row']}>
                    <span class={styles['field-label']}>Emergency Contact</span>
                    <span class={styles['blank-phone']}
                      ><span class={`${styles['blank-value']} ${styles['blank-value-phone']}`}>(555) 214-0193</span
                      ></span
                    >
                  </div>
                  <div class={`${styles['field-row']} ${styles['field-row-last']}`}>
                    <span class={styles['field-label']}>Allergies / Medical</span>
                    <span class={styles['blank-allergies']}
                      ><span class={`${styles['blank-value']} ${styles['blank-value-allergies']}`}>Peanut allergy</span
                      ></span
                    >
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class={styles.checks}>
                  <div class={styles.check}>
                    <span class={styles['check-box-1']}
                      ><svg class={styles['check-mark-1']} viewBox="0 0 18 18" focusable="false"
                        ><path pathLength="1" d="M3 9 L7.5 13.5 L15 4.5"></path></svg
                      ></span
                    >
                    <span class={styles['check-label']}>My child has permission to attend</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class={styles.check}>
                    <span class={styles['check-box-2']}
                      ><svg class={styles['check-mark-2']} viewBox="0 0 18 18" focusable="false"
                        ><path pathLength="1" d="M3 9 L7.5 13.5 L15 4.5"></path></svg
                      ></span
                    >
                    <span class={styles['check-label']}>Photos may be taken during the trip</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p class={styles['confirm-line']}>Sign below to give permission.</p>
                <div class={styles['sig-line']}>
                  <span class={styles['sig-label']}>Parent or Guardian</span>
                  <svg class={styles.sig} viewBox="0 0 220 70" preserveAspectRatio="none" focusable="false">
                    <path
                      pathLength="1"
                      d="M8,50 C14,20 20,15 26,35 C30,50 34,55 38,40 C40,25 46,18 50,30 C54,45 55,52 60,45 L66,20 C70,10 74,10 76,20 L80,45 C84,55 90,55 92,40 C96,20 100,15 104,25 C108,38 112,45 118,35 C124,22 130,18 136,28 C142,42 148,48 156,38 C162,30 168,26 176,32 C184,40 192,44 204,30"
                    ></path>
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <div class={styles['date-line']}>
                  <span class={styles['date-line-label']}>Date</span>
                  <span class={styles['date-line-value']}>05/14</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class={`${styles.layer} ${styles['share-layer']}`}>
              <div class={styles['share-scrim']} aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <div class={styles['share-sheet']}>
                <div class={styles['share-handle']} aria-hidden="true"></div>
                <div class={styles['tool-chips']} aria-hidden="true">
                  <span class={`${styles['tool-chip']} ${styles['tool-chip-share']}`}>Share</span>
                </div>
                <div class={styles['share-file-row']}>
                  <svg class={styles['pdf-icon']} viewBox="0 0 24 28" focusable="false">
                    <path class={styles['pdf-body']} d="M3 1h13l5 5v20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H3a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V2a1 1 0 0 1 1-1z" />
                    <path class={styles['pdf-fold']} d="M16 1v5h5" />
                    <rect class={styles['pdf-tag']} x="3" y="16" width="15" height="7" rx="1.5" />
                    <text class={styles['pdf-tag-text']} x="10.5" y="21.2" text-anchor="middle">PDF</text>
                  </svg>
                  <span class={styles['file-meta']}>
                    <span class={styles['file-name']}>field-trip-permission-slip.pdf</span>
                    <span class={styles['file-size']}>Signed - 248 KB</span>
                  </span>
                </div>
                <div class={styles['share-targets']}>
                  <span class={styles['share-target']}>
                    <span class={styles['share-target-icon']} aria-hidden="true">
                      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" focusable="false">
                        <path
                          fill="none"
                          stroke="currentColor"
                          stroke-width="1.6"
                          stroke-linecap="round"
                          stroke-linejoin="round"
                          d="M4 5h16v10H9l-4 4V5z"
                        ></path>
                      </svg>
                    </span>
                    <span>Messages</span>
                  </span>
                  <span class={styles['share-target']}>
                    <span class={styles['share-target-icon']} aria-hidden="true">
                      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" focusable="false">
                        <rect x="4" y="6" width="16" height="12" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"
                        ></rect>
                        <path
                          fill="none"
                          stroke="currentColor"
                          stroke-width="1.6"
                          stroke-linecap="round"
                          stroke-linejoin="round"
                          d="M4 7l8 6 8-6"
                        ></path>
                      </svg>
                    </span>
                    <span>Mail</span>
                  </span>
                  <span class={styles['share-target']}>
                    <span class={styles['share-target-icon']} aria-hidden="true">
                      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" focusable="false">
                        <circle cx="6" cy="12" r="1.6" fill="currentColor"></circle>
                        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1.6" fill="currentColor"></circle>
                        <circle cx="18" cy="12" r="1.6" fill="currentColor"></circle>
                      </svg>
                    </span>
                    <span>More</span>
                  </span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>


  <div class={`${styles.track} ${styles['track-short']}`} data-hero-track="blur">
    <p class="sr-only">
      An email asks for a copy of a utility bill. Opening it shows several lines of billing
      details. As the page scrolls, the customer ID blurs until it can't be read, the account
      number is blacked out, one line is erased to blank paper, and an unrelated row is deleted so
      the rows below close up. The cleaned-up document is then attached to a reply and sent.
    </p>
    <div class={styles.stage} data-hero-stage>
      <h3 class={`type-card ${styles.caption}`}>Some of it is nobody's business. Blur it out before you reply.</h3>
      <div class={styles['progress-rail']} aria-hidden="true">
        <span class={`${styles['progress-seg']} ${styles['progress-seg-done']}`}></span>
        <span class={`${styles['progress-seg']} ${styles['progress-seg-current']}`}></span>
      </div>
      <div class={styles.phone} aria-hidden="true">
        <div class={styles.screen}>
          <div class={styles['status-bar']}>
            <span>9:41</span>
            <span class={styles['status-icons']}>
              <svg class={styles['icon-airplane']} viewBox="0 0 24 24" focusable="false">
                <path
                  fill="currentColor"
                  d="M21 16v-2l-8-5V3.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-3 0V9l-8 5v2l8-2.5V19l-2.5 2v1.5l3.5-1 3.5 1V21l-2.5-2v-5.5z"
                />
              </svg>
              <svg class={styles['icon-battery']} viewBox="0 0 24 12" focusable="false">
                <rect x="1" y="1" width="19" height="10" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" />
                <rect x="21" y="4" width="2" height="4" rx="1" fill="currentColor" />
                <rect x="3" y="3" width="14" height="6" rx="1" fill="currentColor" />
              </svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class={styles.layers}>
            <div class={`${styles.layer} ${styles['email-layer']}`}>
              <div class={styles['panel-head']}>Inbox</div>
              <div class={`${styles['email-row']} ${styles['anim-arrive']}`}>
                <span class={styles.avatar}>FD</span>
                <span class={styles['email-meta']}>
                  <span class={styles['email-from']}>Front Desk</span>
                  <span class={styles['email-subject']}>Quick favor, need that bill on file</span>
                  <span class={styles['email-preview']}
                    >Hi, could you send a copy of your utility bill for our records?</span
                  >
                </span>
              </div>
              <div class={styles['email-row-muted']}>
                <span class={styles.avatar}>TM</span>
                <span class={styles['email-meta']}>
                  <span class={styles['email-from']}>Team</span>
                  <span class={styles['email-subject']}>Lunch on Friday?</span>
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class={`${styles.layer} ${styles['bill-layer']}`}>
              <div class={styles['panel-head']}>utility-bill.pdf</div>
              <div class={styles['tool-chips']} aria-hidden="true">
                <span class={`${styles['tool-chip']} ${styles['tool-chip-blur']}`}>Blur</span>
                <span class={`${styles['tool-chip']} ${styles['tool-chip-blackout']}`}>Blackout</span>
                <span class={`${styles['tool-chip']} ${styles['tool-chip-whiteout']}`}>Whiteout</span>
                <span class={`${styles['tool-chip']} ${styles['tool-chip-delete']}`}>Delete</span>
              </div>
              <div class={styles['doc-body']}>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}><span>Account Holder</span><span>J. Alvarez</span></div>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}><span>Service Address</span><span>14 Maple Court</span></div>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}><span>Billing Period</span><span>Jul 1 to Aug 1</span></div>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}>
                  <span>Customer ID</span>
                  <span class={styles['blur-value']}>302-45-6789</span>
                </div>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}>
                  <span>Account No</span>
                  <span class={styles['redact-wrap']}>
                    <span class={styles['redact-value']}>0001 1488 25</span>
                    <span class={styles['blackout-bar']} aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  </span>
                </div>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}><span>Rate Plan</span><span>Residential Standard</span></div>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}>
                  <span>Meter Serial</span>
                  <span class={styles['redact-wrap']}>
                    <span class={styles['redact-value']}>MTR-88291</span>
                    <span class={styles['whiteout-bar']} aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  </span>
                </div>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}><span>Meter Reading, Prior</span><span>04821</span></div>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}><span>Meter Reading, Current</span><span>05114</span></div>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}><span>Usage</span><span>293 kWh</span></div>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}>
                  <span class={styles['delete-row-text']}>Late Fee Note</span>
                  <span class={styles['delete-row-text']}>Includes $12 reminder fee</span>
                </div>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}><span>Amount Due</span><span>$104.20</span></div>
                <div class={styles['doc-line']}><span>Due Date</span><span>Sep 28</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class={`${styles.layer} ${styles['reply-layer']} ${styles['layer-final']}`}>
              <div class={styles['panel-head']}>Reply</div>
              <div class={styles['reply-body']}>
                <p class={styles['reply-text']}>Here you go.</p>
                <div class={styles['attach-chip']}>
                  <span class={styles['blur-dot']} aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class={styles['attach-name']}>utility-bill.pdf</span>
                  <span class={styles['attach-tag']}>cleaned</span>
                </div>
                <div class={`${styles['send-btn']} ${styles['anim-send']}`}>Send</div>
              </div>
              <div class={`${styles['sent-label']} ${styles['anim-sent']}`}>Sent</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class={styles.outro}>
    <p>Turn on airplane mode and give it a try. It still works.</p>
  </div>
</section>
